 (log
  (((agent "xl1")
    (kind note)
    (seq 165)
    (text
     "anchors.rkt: python files resolve via python.rkt's find-anchor worker (ast, qualname = dotted path like Class.method), replacing the heuristic. Span = first decorator through end_lineno; hash = ast.dump(include_attributes=False) so formatting/comments/whitespace are invisible but a real body/decorator/rename change is not. Ambiguous bare names (e.g. 3 classes each with __init__) return not-found with the qualified candidates listed, rather than silently picking the first (the old heuristic's failure mode). Overload/singledispatch/property-setter groups resolve to the first definition and report how many later ones share the name ('shadowed). tests/unit-test.rkt's old .py heuristic example now correctly uses the python method; moved that regression case to Ruby to keep heuristic coverage.")
